1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
We are Abed and Mohamad, team ZENITH LABS.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Pluto was found by blinking two photos. We
blink SPHEREx.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,500
This is ParallaX: see what really moved or
changed in the infrared.

4
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:15,500
SPHEREx never repeats a colour, so stars
become false alarms.

5
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:20,500
From NASA’s open data, we predict each
frame’s own colours, and subtract.

6
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:25,000
Next: anyone types coordinates and
explores the changing sky.

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,500
ParallaX: open source, open data.

